{
 "summary": "The evidence does not support a root cause. Gateway, inventory and orders all show a 0% 5xx ratio and normal p95 latency (gateway max 182ms) across the window, which contradicts a server-side outage in these services. Traces, logs and deployment records returned nothing, and no checkout-specific or payment service metrics were collected, so the failure may lie outside the observed services or not appear as HTTP 5xx.",
 "root_cause": null,
 "contributing_factors": [],
 "timeline": [],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "A server-side error cascade through gateway is not supported. Gateway shows a 0% 5xx ratio (avg and max) and p95 latency of at most 182ms throughout the window.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory is not failing or slow. It shows a 0% 5xx ratio and p95 latency of about 45-47ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5859ba914c39"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders is not failing or slow. It shows a 0% 5xx ratio and p95 latency of at most 100ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Deployment records were queried and returned nothing in the window, so no deploy-related lead is available.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "No metrics exist for a checkout, payment, or cart service. If checkout is handled by a service outside gateway, inventory and orders, its health is unobserved.",
  "Only 5xx ratios are measured. Checkout failures could be returned as 4xx, as 200 responses carrying error bodies, or could happen client-side or in front of the gateway (CDN, DNS, load balancer), and none of these would show up here.",
  "Gateway request rate ended at 1.56 req/s against a 2.24 req/s max. Without a baseline it is unclear whether checkout traffic is failing to reach the gateway at all.",
  "Traces and logs returned nothing even though the services are serving about 1-2 req/s. This may point to an instrumentation or pipeline gap rather than a real absence of activity.",
  "No deployment records were found, and it is unknown whether config, feature flag, or third-party (e.g. payment provider) changes happened in the window.",
  "The customer-facing impact has not been confirmed (synthetic checks, support reports, frontend errors)."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Reproduce a checkout end-to-end (synthetic or manual) and capture the HTTP status, response body and which hop fails.",
   "rationale": "Server metrics show no errors, so the failure point has to be located directly.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Query 4xx rates and per-route metrics on gateway for the checkout endpoint, and collect metrics for any checkout or payment services and external payment provider status.",
   "rationale": "The only error signal collected is 5xx on three services. Checkout-specific routes and dependencies are unobserved.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check edge components in front of gateway (CDN, DNS, load balancer, frontend/JS errors) and compare gateway traffic to a normal baseline.",
   "rationale": "Gateway is healthy but its request rate is modest and falling at the end of the window, which is consistent with requests not reaching it.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Re-run the trace and log queries with a wider window and verify that the collection pipelines are healthy.",
   "rationale": "Both sources returned nothing despite live traffic, so key diagnostic data is missing.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-traces",
    "src-logs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Look for config, feature-flag, or infrastructure changes not captured in the deployment records, and widen the deployment query window.",
   "rationale": "No deployment records were found, but changes outside the deploy pipeline could still explain the outage.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
